amendments.amended_content:
CORRECTION (entities-omission corpus repair, phase 3, 2026-11-19): The DeclaredReferentConflictRejected rejection described below was a DEFECT, and it is now FIXED. Task 6059 landed on main in merge commit 1ac3835e85 on 2026-10-18. Since then fused-memory/src/fused_memory/utils/referent_resolution.py::_conflicting_referents treats the scanner's silence about a declared task as uninformative per referent: a declaration is rejected only on positive evidence (a near-miss typo of a scanned task number that the content never writes, or the declared number under another project), and an add_memory whose explicit category discards the declaration (a Mem0-primary write without dual_write) is never conflict-rejected. The one residual 6059 left, prose of the form "word: NNNN" scanned as a project-qualified referent, was fixed by task 6826 (merge commit b5cc350565, 2026-11-18). Declaring `entities` is the expected default. Keep declaring; if a write is rejected, fix the wrong id, or write that task as "task NNN" in the content. Do NOT omit `entities`: on a Graphiti-primary write, omitting it misattributes the memory to whichever task the scanner could see, and the declaration rate is the adoption signal of plans/memory-referent-fidelity-prd.md decision 4. This repair is task 6060 (phase 1), task 6067 (phase 2) and task 7117 (phase 3).

add_memory `entities` gotcha (fused-memory, measured 2026-10-09): the content scan recognises a task referent only in the form "task N" / "Task N" (and "tasks N"-style prose that it parses). It does NOT count:
- bare ids in parentheses ("α (6524)", "ζ 6529");
- ranges ("6524–6528");
- slash pairs ("tasks 4082/6578": only the first was seen);
- escalation ids ("esc-4681-3").

Declaring any of those in `entities` is REJECTED as DeclaredReferentConflictRejected. The fix is to write "task 6524" in the prose (do NOT drop ids from `entities` — see the correction above).

